# The composition root's own group. authority-url is a literal, so the group's
# name survives a resolution that drops every reference — which is exactly why
# a parity assertion over group NAMES cannot see a lost value, and why the
# tests below assert the value.
#
# authority-endpoint is the root-only reference, and it names platform/authority
# on purpose: no service declares this group except platform/gateway, and no
# declared group of any service names that producer. Producer discovery driven
# by the declared groups alone therefore never binds its mappings for
# payments/api or payments/worker, and core drops the value for them, silently
# (cli#882). Naming platform/gateway here instead would hide the fault for
# payments/api, whose declared `payments-store` names that same producer and so
# binds it either way.
authority-url=https://authority.example
authority-endpoint=${endpoint:platform/authority/rest}
# A credential-named value: a root group's credential renders as a secretKeyRef,
# which is the consequence an operator meets (TestACompositionRootCredential...).
authority-token=plaintext-only-in-the-fixture
